# lakehouse.env — owner-only secrets and credentials for v2 HF operations.
#
# This is a TEMPLATE. Copy it to a file OUTSIDE the repository (the owner keeps it at D:\Development\lakehouse.env),
# fill the values, and never commit the filled file. The deploy runbook (docs/ops/deploy.md) and the token checker
# (scripts/check_hf_token.py --token-env <NAME>) read these by variable name. A session never prints these values.
#
# Not every key is needed for every task — each comment says when.

# --- HF tokens -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Ops Space DATA token: fine-grained, Write on luxury-lakehouse/lake ONLY (no restricted, no -control).
# Verify: uv run python scripts/check_hf_token.py space --token-env HF_TOKEN --lake luxury-lakehouse/lake \
#   --restricted luxury-lakehouse/restricted --control luxury-lakehouse/lake-control --read-only
HF_TOKEN=

# The Ops Space JOB-CONTROL token: a classic WRITE-role token (a personal-namespace scheduled job cannot be managed by
# a fine-grained token — HF fine-grained Jobs is org-only). The Settings schedule reads it. Set it as the Space secret
# of the same name. Verify: uv run python scripts/check_hf_token.py jobs --token-env LAKEHOUSE_HF_JOBS_TOKEN --job-id <id>
LAKEHOUSE_HF_JOBS_TOKEN=

# The hf_space TEST token: fine-grained, Write on luxury-lakehouse/lake-test ONLY. Mirrors the Ops Space data token.
# Verify: uv run python scripts/check_hf_token.py space --token-env HF_LAKE_TEST --lake luxury-lakehouse/lake-test \
#   --restricted luxury-lakehouse/restricted-test --control luxury-lakehouse/lake-test-control
HF_LAKE_TEST=

# --- HF S3 gateway key (Job / hf_job only) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated in the HF web UI: Access Tokens -> the Job token's menu -> "Generate S3 credentials". The secret shows once.
# The key inherits the Job token's Write scope. Pass with --secrets-file to hf jobs.
HF_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
HF_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Provider tokens -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The pining OWNER token (full access). Used by the Job and local pining ingests.
PINING_FOR_THE_DATA_TOKEN=

# The pining LIST-ONLY token (lists private pining tournaments; optional). Set as the Ops Space secret of the same name.
PINING_LIST_TOKEN=

# A GitHub token to raise the rate limit for the GitHub sources (statsbomb_public, skillcorner_public). Optional.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Identifiers (not secrets, handy to keep together) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner-created scheduled job id (also the Ops Space variable LAKEHOUSE_HF_SCHEDULED_JOB_ID). Used by the jobs check.
LAKEHOUSE_HF_SCHEDULED_JOB_ID=
